  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of immediate lifesaving emergency Shelter, non-food items (NFI) and Camp Coordination and Camp Management assistance in response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy&#x2019;s impact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This IOM project provides immediate lifesaving emergency Shelter, non-food items (NFI), and Camp Coordination and Camp Management assistance in response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy&#x2019;s impact. IOM provides basic emergency shelter and NFIs kits, addressing the most urgent needs of 2,500 households. IOM offers support to coordination efforts on the provision of Shelter and NFI assistance in the country, working in close coordination with co-leads of the Shelter, NFI and CCCM Cluster. The project provides humanitarian assistance to  28,900 people, including  5,202 women, 3,468 men,  3,468 children, and including 289 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
